        _qa("What is IR1?", "IR1 is the atomic input register. It represents the smallest current text unit, normally the final character or symbol, together with useful character identity such as Unicode/code-point, hexadecimal, binary, or tokenizer-facing representation. IR1 answers: what exact symbol am I looking at?"),
        _qa("What is IR2?", "IR2 is the local textual continuity register. It represents a short neighboring sequence such as the final two characters or another deliberately bounded local window. IR2 helps detect word boundaries, punctuation relationships, escapes, adjacent symbols, and immediate textual continuity. IR2 is not the NPU and must not be called L2."),
        _qa("What is IR3?", "IR3 is the mathematical and symbolic interpretation register: a bounded mini imagination simulator for the current input. It may translate letters or symbols into hexadecimal, decimal, positional, frequency, coordinate, or other numerical properties; detect operators and sequences; stage a calculation; or form a mathematical hypothesis about a recurrently unresolved pattern."),
        _qa("What modes can IR3 use?", "IR3 may classify a candidate as IR3_TEXT when mathematics only supports a linguistic explanation, IR3_CALC when the input specifies a sufficiently determinate computation, or IR3_THEORY when mathematical structure can generate candidate interpretations without one established answer."),
        _qa("When should IR3 activate?", "IR3 may activate immediately for explicit numbers, equations, hexadecimal, coordinates, ratios, symbolic patterns, or calculation requests. It may also be consulted when ordinary linguistic interpretation repeatedly fails and the unresolved structure plausibly represents a mathematical or encoded relation. Recurrent failure is a clue, not proof."),
        _qa("When should IR3 not force a calculation?", "Do not calculate merely because a sentence contains mathematical vocabulary. First distinguish a request for a numeric result from a request for prose, theory, analogy, definition, code, or discussion. IR3 can support those tasks without replacing them."),
        _qa("Can IR3 invent a possible interpretation?", "Yes, but a generated interpretation begins as a hypothesis or UNKNOWN/MAYBE candidate unless evidence supports a stronger state. A mathematical imagination is not automatically a fact, definition, or durable memory entry."),
        _qa("How do IR1 IR2 and IR3 differ from L1 L2 and L3?", "IR1, IR2, and IR3 are transient model-facing input registers. L1, L2, and L3 are AItech hardware/cache-routing layers: L1 GPU fast prediction state, L2 NPU intermediate processing state, and L3 CPU general-control/fallback state. Never reuse the old L1/L2 character-register meaning."),
        _qa("Should transient IR state be learned as permanent truth?", "No. IR state can guide the current inference and can provide examples for training, but ephemeral character, calculation, or routing state must not automatically become a durable fact. Promote only the resulting reusable interpretation when semantic evidence warrants it."),
    ]
    return "\n".join(lines)


