def build_hardware_ledger_graph():
    """Teach L1 GPU / L2 NPU / L3 CPU runtime cache hierarchy, daemon state, and live ledgers."""
    lines = [
        "<|system|> AItech hardware-cache map. L1/L2/L3 are runtime hardware-routing concepts. They are distinct from IR1/IR2/IR3 input registers. <|endoftext|>",
        _qa("What is the L1 L2 L3 hardware hierarchy?", "L1 is the GPU fast prediction and immediate scheduling layer; L2 is the NPU intermediate processing, reflection, sorting, and ingestion layer; L3 is the CPU general-control, fallback, clutch, and halt layer. The labels describe AItech's hardware-inspired runtime organization and must not be reused for character registers."),
        _qa("What is L1 GPU state?", "L1_GPU lives under session.noq/dgapi/gpu/. predictions.txt is its current or last-known ranked processing ledger and characters.txt is the manual tokenizer patch registry. L1 answers what work or prediction state should receive immediate attention when that information is relevant."),
        _qa("What is L2 NPU state?", "L2_NPU lives under session.noq/dgapi/npu/. It holds queued material for deterministic ingestion and may receive bounded self-reflection or intermediate cognitive material through L2 routing. L2 is an intermediate processing surface, not automatically durable semantic memory."),
        _qa("What is L3 CPU state?", "L3_CPU lives under session.noq/dgapi/cpu/. It provides general-control and fallback semantics and contains kqkkqq.txt, the CPU clutch tripwire. A halt or axed state can suspend background processing when runtime control requires it."),
        _qa("How should hardware cache state be interpreted while the daemon is active?", "Treat current ledgers and routing files as live operational context when relevant to inference, scheduling, NPU work, hardware state, training, or debugging. Read only the bounded state needed for the current operation and keep it distinct from durable factual memory."),
        _qa("How should hardware cache state be interpreted while the daemon is inactive?", "Existing files may still describe useful last-known state, history, or queued work, but they are not evidence that processing is currently active. Mark the interpretation as retained or potentially stale and use it for inspection, recovery, or context only when relevant."),
        _qa("When should hardware cache state not be injected?", "Do not consume prompt context merely because a ledger file exists. Ordinary conversation that does not depend on hardware scheduling, queued NPU work, cache priority, runtime control, training, or debugging can omit transient cache state. Task relevance takes priority over unconditional injection."),
        _qa("What is dgapi/gpu/predictions.txt?", "predictions.txt is written by disk_orchestrator.py after it evaluates files in the npu directory. It opens with the header [ 1/2 TOKEN INSTRUCTION LEDGER ] and each row reads N. filename | Typographic Mass: M | Latency: S. Rows are ordered by typographic mass descending, with the filename as a deterministic tiebreak, so the ledger is reproducible for identical inputs. The runtime can use it as L1 scheduling context and to ingest NPU files in that order."),
        _qa("What is dgapi/gpu/characters.txt?", "characters.txt is the manual tokenizer patch registry. Each line can associate a hexadecimal code, symbol, name, timestamp, and weight. Tokenizer patch logic can use it to teach symbols as atomic concepts. This registry belongs to the GPU hardware area but is not IR1 itself."),
        _qa("What is the NPU ingestion flow?", "First disk_orchestrator evaluates files in L2_NPU and sequences them. Second it writes the order to L1_GPU predictions.txt. Third the runtime ingests the files in that order and moves completed material to intake/processed. L3_CPU clutch state can halt the pipeline when required."),
        _qa("What does an L2_ROUTE tag mean?", "L2_ROUTE marks bounded generated material intended for intermediate NPU-side reflection, sorting, or later ingestion. Routing something to L2 does not establish it as a fact and does not require it to be shown to the user as ordinary response text."),
        _qa("What does an L3_HALT tag mean?", "L3_HALT is runtime control intent for the CPU clutch/fallback layer. It is not ordinary conversational content and should not be learned as a semantic proposition merely because the tag appeared in generated text."),
    ]
    predictions_path = "session.noq/dgapi/gpu/predictions.txt"
    if os.path.exists(predictions_path):
        try:
            pred_content = open(predictions_path, encoding="utf-8").read().strip()
            if pred_content:
                lines.append(_qa("What is currently recorded in the L1 predictions ledger?", f"[L1_RETAINED_OR_LIVE_STATE] {pred_content[:500]}"))
        except Exception:
            pass
    return "\n".join(lines)


