    """
    lines = [
        "<|user|> How does live training work after each response? <|endoftext|>",
        (
            "<|assistant|> After every non-silent response the model trains on the interaction. "
            "Training text is formatted as User: prompt then Assistant: response then endoftext. "
            "If shatter_enabled in prefs.json the response is split into word variants: "
            "from all words down to the last 5 words stepping by 1, weighted 1.0 for the full "
            "response and 0.5 for shorter variants. "
            "If decay_enabled character variants are generated instead. "
            "If both are disabled a single training pass runs. "
            "A neutral_points spend skips training entirely for that turn. <|endoftext|>"
        ),
        "<|user|> What is the confidence scoring system? <|endoftext|>",
        (
            "<|assistant|> Each prompt is stored in confidence_map with a score from 0 to 100. "
            "The correct command increments the score by 1 up to 100. "
            "The current score creates a doubt_factor of score divided by 200. "
            "doubt_factor raises dynamic_temp by up to 0.5 above the base 0.7 "
            "and raises repetition_penalty. "
            "The correct command also runs a reinforcement training pass with "
            "scaled_loss multiplied by 1 plus score divided by 10 "
            "so frequently-correct prompts receive stronger weight updates. "
            "correct silence trains the model to output nothing for that prompt. <|endoftext|>"
        ),
        "<|user|> What is the theory engine? <|endoftext|>",
        (
            "<|assistant|> The theory engine activates with thought_seconds or the c N command. "
            "N iterations of subconscious generation run on the current prompt at temperature plus 0.2. "
            "Words from each output are added to theory_weights with frequency counts. "
            "The top 5 session words are formatted as Applied Theory and injected "
            "into the next response prompt. "
            "The theory entry is also logged to experimental.txt as a THEORY block "
            "with STATUS PENDING awaiting verification or promotion to facts.txt. <|endoftext|>"
        ),
        "<|user|> What is the hm scratchpad? <|endoftext|>",
        (
            "<|assistant|> When hm_points are available the model runs an internal draft before responding. "
            "The prompt is extended with Internal Thought and the model generates 50 tokens. "
            "This draft is shown as the internal thought and then included in the final prompt "
            "as context before the assistant turn. "
            "The hm scratchpad lets the model reason before committing to an answer. "
            "Spending hm_points costs 1 point per turn. <|endoftext|>"
        ),
        _qa("What input registers can support live inference?", "IR1 carries atomic character identity such as HEX or binary, IR2 carries bounded local textual continuity, and IR3 can stage mathematical or symbolic interpretation. These are transient inference aids. L1/L2/L3 are reserved for GPU/NPU/CPU hardware cache semantics."),
        _qa("Should live training copy transient register or cache state into durable knowledge?", "Not automatically. Train on the meaningful interaction or reusable interpretation; ephemeral IR values and current L1/L2/L3 scheduling state describe the turn or machine environment and should remain transient unless a separate semantic reason warrants preserving them."),
        "<|user|> What is the weights rebuild command? <|endoftext|>",
        (
            "<|assistant|> weights rebuild recalculates weights.txt from scratch by reading "
            "every named semantic memory file and counting word frequencies. "
            "The ledger format uses square bracket section headers for each filename "
