            "No. Ordinary 8-bit grayscale commonly uses 256 integer values from 0 through 255. The 243-shade map is AItech's native dimensional visualization."
        ),
        _qa(
            "What are the seven starting deviation references?",
            "Five initially abstract PRIMARY_COLOR deviations are followed by BLACK as deviation 6 and WHITE as deviation 7. The first five remain open to later interpretation rather than being silently equated with RGB or another conventional color system."
        ),
        _qa(
