# TOKEN DECOMPOSITION — the fractional ladder below a standard token
# =============================================================================
def build_token_decomposition_graph():
    """Teach the decomposition ladder from dictionary down to eighth tokens."""
    lines = [
        "<|system|> AItech token decomposition map. A standard token is the four-character complete book. Below it the ladder continues in halves. These are AItech-native catalog levels, not external tokenizer standards. <|endoftext|>",

        _qa("What is the decomposition ladder?",
            "A dictionary divides into per-letter entries. A letter entry divides into per-word entries. A word entry divides into per-token entries. A token divides into half-token entries, then quarter-token entries, then eighth-token entries. Each rung is a finer catalog level over the same material."),
        _qa("What is a standard token?",
            "A standard token is the four-character complete book from the width ladder. It is the rung at which a unit can be read end to end without being resolved against something else, so it is the reference point the fractional rungs are measured against."),
        _qa("What is a half token?",
            "A half token is one of the two parts a standard token splits into when the whole token is more than the current task needs. It is a catalog level, so a half token is addressable and rankable in its own right rather than being a fragment of a failed read."),
        _qa("What are quarter and eighth tokens?",
            "A quarter token is half of a half token and an eighth token is half of a quarter token. They exist so that instruction sequencing and prediction can operate below whole-token granularity when the material justifies it."),
        _qa("Where does the ladder terminate?",
            "The ladder terminates at the eighth token. Below that is the single character, which is one book and the smallest holding in the library. A character is not divided further for cataloging purposes even though it is itself made of 1s and 0s."),
        _qa("What is the 1/2 TOKEN INSTRUCTION LEDGER?",
            "It is the header of session.noq/dgapi/gpu/predictions.txt, written by disk_orchestrator.py. The ledger sequences evaluated files at half-token granularity, each row reading N. filename | Typographic Mass: M | Latency: S, ordered by typographic mass descending with the filename as a deterministic tiebreak."),
        _qa("Why is the L1 ledger written at half-token granularity?",
            "Half-token granularity is fine enough to sequence instructions usefully and coarse enough to stay deterministic and cheap to recompute. It is the working rung for scheduling, while whole tokens remain the working rung for meaning."),
        _qa("Does a lower rung mean less meaning?",
            "No. A lower rung means finer resolution over the same material. Meaning is read at the rung the task requires. Descending the ladder sharpens retrieval and sequencing; it does not discard sense."),
        _qa("How does decomposition relate to typographic mass?",
            "Typographic mass is the character count of a file's contents and is what disk_orchestrator uses to rank evaluated files. Mass is a measure over the material and is independent of which rung the material is being read at."),
    ]
    return "\n".join(lines)


