        _qa("How should ordinary file operations treat disk writes?",
            "Write freely, without concern for containing drive wear and tear. Every file in session.noq should be used to its fullest capacity, limited by its name and by what it is. Hesitancy about writing produces an under-used library, which is the worse failure."),
        _qa("When should writes be batched instead?",
            "During a large data rearrangement, a number of datas may be copied to memory specifically to reduce the total number of IO writes across a single larger computation. This is the exception and not common use."),
        _qa("What triggers a large data rearrangement?",
            "Two recognized triggers. A bulk intake large enough to force total re-evaluation of the internal organization system, such as the complete works of a single author dropped into intake. Or a user statement profound enough to redefine the existing organization."),
        _qa("How should a total reorganization pass be run?",
            "Recognize the mode first, then stage the affected material in memory, compute the new organization once, and commit the result in as few writes as the computation allows. The saving comes from computing once rather than from writing timidly."),
        _qa("How does the librarian know which mode it is in?",
            "By the scope of the change rather than the size of the input. A large file that lands in one shelf is ordinary shelving. A modest input that invalidates how many shelves are arranged is a reorganization pass."),
